text:
Priya Shah: FYI opening a docs PR to add a small migration guide for Dedicated -> Reserved Pools, plus two runnable snippets (Terraform + Node). PR: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/448
Ben Cho: great. can you include an explicit example of switching an existing pool to `reserved = true` and the implications for SLA/eviction? folks keep asking that.
Priya Shah: yes. planning a short 'What changes' section: note that reserved pools get capacity guarantees but still may be drained for emergency maintenance. proposed wording: "Reserved pools have higher availability guarantees; however, during platform maintenance we may perform best-effort migrations or failover to compatible model variants. See SLA matrix for details."
Jason Li: add a tiny table row showing "Eviction behavior" -> "maintenance: best-effort migration; emergency: possible eviction with audit logs". keep it non-legal.
Evan Kim: for the Terraform snippet I ran into a controller validation error if the annotation key is `isolate: true`. Use the controller-backed annotation `redwood.org/pool-isolation: tenant`. otherwise the operator will reject the object.
Priya Shah: good catch. will change. current TF snippet draft:
```hcl
provider "redwood" {
  region = "eu-central-1"
}
resource "redwood_dedicated_capacity_pool" "emails" {
  reserved = true
  annotations = {
    "redwood.org/pool-isolation" = "tenant"
  }
  autoscale {
    min_replicas = 1
    max_replicas = 6
    policy = "cost_efficiency"
  }
}
```
Ben Cho: small ask: add a one-line note explaining `cost_efficiency` vs `latency_slo` policies and when to choose each.
Maddy Nguyen: I'll add a Node SDK snippet for configuring autoscale and a Python variant in comments. Node example suggestion:
```js
const client = new RedwoodClient();
await client.pools.update("emails", {
  reserved: true,
  annotations: { "redwood.org/pool-isolation": "tenant" },
  autoscale: { min: 1, max: 6, policy: "cost_efficiency" }
});
```
Jason Li: perfect. can we also surface the preview link when staging builds? makes reviews quicker.
docs-bot: Preview deployed: https://deploy-preview-448--docs.redwood.ai/dedicated/reserved-migration (staging)
Evan Kim: bumped into a kube-controller bug when testing autoscale.policy = "cost_efficiency" on older agents (see https://github.com/redwood-inference/infra/issues/912). I linked a workaround in the PR comments (restart controller after CRD update).
Priya Shah: thanks Evan, I'll link that issue and include a short troubleshooting section. also adding a note to check provider block in TF (people forget it).
Ben Cho: wording LGTM after those changes. keep the SLA line high level and link to SLA matrix for legal language.
Maddy Nguyen: will do final pass on snippets and merge after Ben + Jason approve.
docs-bot: PR merged by Priya Shah — live deploy started :rocket:
